        { "text": "$x=12$ or $x=2$", "why": "Forgot to divide the numerator by $2a=4$." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$2x-7=-\\frac{3}{x}$\n$2x^{2}-7x=-3$\n$2x^{2}-7x+3=0$\n$a=2$, $b=-7$, $c=3$\n$x=\\frac{-(-7)\\pm\\sqrt{(-7)^{2}-4(2)(3)}}{2(2)}$\n$=\\frac{7\\pm\\sqrt{25}}{4}$\n$=\\frac{7\\pm5}{4}$\n$x=3$ or $x=\\frac{1}{2}$"
